{"title":"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the measure of the largest angle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(angle PQR = 6x, angle PRQ = x, angle QPR = 3x)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf4e9dae3585f311c83f434f28616c5fba6f2b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 144^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 96^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 120^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 60^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 108^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"499\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the interior angles in any triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />. From the diagram, this means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/2/742d57b7fd85e96ba98d360d8a597470b660c0af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\circ} + 3x^{\\circ} + 6x^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"178\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba08339fa80df8c0b5e4572233ee5d2d41895ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10x^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6e35f4a653bd9f678a3438e026b00bae7c8826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{180^{\\circ}}{10^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d3e4315e912987aa3b30ed98d1a76b68101997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Using the diagram, we also see that the largest angle was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94aef9d098dc8811c41678e4886170337afb709e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d3e4315e912987aa3b30ed98d1a76b68101997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> into this, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e82352fb427a3c7310c3f0965d8102960e25acb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 18^{\\circ} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 108^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley\">2010 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=201